            "review_title": "Review at Quyen Quyen Restaurant",
            "review_text": "739heidi73\nBrisbane, Australia1 contribution\n0\nGreat spot to sample authentic vietnamese food.\nJul 2015 • Couples\nWe came on this restaurant by accident, having walked around the busy roundabout looking for somewhere to eat only to be blasted by loud music everywhere. When we walked in to Quyen Quyen we were a bit apprehensive as it was all locals, the waiters didn't speak English, however a nice Vietnamese man by the name of Minh stood up from his table of friends, told us to come on in, great food and great prices he said, he proceeded to get the owner for us to explain the menu. The owner again a very friendly man called Viet came and spoke to us, he explained it was their last night of operation(Fri 31st July) as they were moving to new premises, there wasn't a menu as such that night but he explained what dishes they did have and we trusted his pick for us. The food was delicious, highland style, quite hot and spicy, beautiful free range pork belly, spicy beef, a saute mushroom and vegetable dish(which he gave us on the house).\nIt turned out Viet is from Canberra, Australia and had been back in Vietnam for the past 5 years. Our friendly locals on the other table continued to chat to us through the evening and even shouted us a bottle of Fruit Wine made in The Highlands to take back to Australia with us.\nWhat a fantastic evening, meeting great people, these are the moments you remember!!\nDefinitely a must visit in Ho Chi Minh if you can find their new premises.\nViet we wish you all the best!!!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 9, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
