            "review_title": "Review at Quyen Quyen Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Jason M\n18 contributions\n0\nBest restaurant so far in HCMC\nMay 2015 • Family\nCame across Quyen Quyen by chance. We were met by a very well spoken gentleman named Viet who told us about his restaurant. \nViet took us in and sat us d9wn and told us about the specialities on offer. \nWe had some free range chicken with bamboo rice, grilled squid with a home made satay sauce (sensational! ), mushrooms wrapped in smoked bacon and sauteed vegetables (baby pumpkin and jungle spinach?) In garlic. Viet even arranged for a small bowl of plain rice for my 18 month old baby girl.\nAll up, the above dishes, 6 beers, 3 soft drinks under $40aud.\nBy far the best place we've eaten in Saigon and we'll definitely be back before we head off!\nHighly recommend to all travellers for a unique culinary experience. \nBe prepared for your taste buds to be blown awsy!\nRead more\nWritten May 24, 2015",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
