            "review_text": "mikkieDee\nSydney, Australia66 contributions\n0\nUnusual and delicious\nApr 2015 • Friends\nWe stumbled across this brightly-lit place, near the 'Lotus flower' roundabout. We were greeted by a very friendly, English-speaking owner called Viet, who told us about the specials for the night. We decided to try all of them, and were very glad we did. Viet explained the food was from the Central highlands: the pork was lean, the beef was slow-roasted, and the chicken was organic. When they arrived, every dish was well-presented and fantastic - all featuring chunky salsas - and one was served with noni berries. The flavours were unlike anything I've tasted here. \nWe also had a lovely sake-like hot drink, made from the berries, and a range of wines his brother makes are available - which we'll try next time. \nI believe the restaurant officially opens on the 8th May, but give it a shot.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 25, 2015",
